==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|tīra-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|dei-|lang=ang}}.

Cognate with Old Norse {{term|tírr||glory, renown|lang=non}}. A variant of {{proto|Germanic|tērīn-|lang=ang}}, gave Old High German {{term|zieri|zierī|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Zier||splendour, beauty|lang=de}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ti:ɹ/|lang=ang}}, {{SAMPA|/ti:r/}}

===Noun===
{{infl|ang|noun|head=tīr|g=m}}

# [[fame]], [[glory]]

